<https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/live/job/arbeitnow-operations-strategy-internship-berlin-132081> a prov:Entity,
        schema:JobPosting ;
    dcterms:source <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/prototypes/kg-jobs/source/arbeitnow> ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-08-19T04:41:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/bunch/operations-strategy-internship-berlin-132081> ;
    kgjobs:active true ;
    kgjobs:canonicalFingerprint "fb67ba1f3a290b25cd9e837d53610c1c8990320db8f2f59c04d5093ea8b0fba2" ;
    kgjobs:classification "not_match" ;
    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-08-19T04:41:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-08-19T04:41:07+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "operations-strategy-internship-berlin-132081" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-19"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "bunch is building the backbone of private markets. We are enabling next-gen fund operations with one integrated system that combines secure data infrastructure, AI-powered workflows and expert fund services. If you value ownership, growth through real responsibility, and working with a thoughtful, ambitious team, this role might be for you. We are looking for an Operations & Strategy Intern on a rolling basis, with a minimum commitment of six months. Are you a motivated student nearing the end of your studies or a recent graduate with a structured mindset, a proactive attitude, or a passion for detail? Do you want to experience how the private markets actually work and help shape how they operate at scale? Then this is your chance to join one of Berlin’s hottest startups in the FinTech space. Your Mission As an Operations & Strategy Intern, you’ll become part of our core Ops team - solving real problems across private market investing. You’ll take ownership in one of four focus areas depending on your strengths and interests, and support process execution, improvement, and scale. While track placement will reflect business needs, you’ll remain part of the broader Ops team with opportunities to explore other areas during your time with us. This is your opportunity to learn fast, work hard, and make your mark. Focus Areas Investor Due Diligence Help us maintain trust with our clients by supporting robust investor onboarding and compliance processes. You’ll work within clearly structured workflows (like KYC/AML checks), flag inconsistencies, and keep our controls running smoothly. Ideal for detail-oriented individuals with a calm, structured working style - and the ability to speak up when it matters. ➡️ Previous experience in banking, law, or regulatory settings is a plus. Where this can take you: Careers in compliance, risk operations or legal/finance operations. Fund Administration Support our fund onboarding process by coordinating investor support, client onboarding, document preparation, and troubleshooting operational issues as funds transition onto our platform. You’ll liaise with internal and external stakeholders, map fund structures, and help ensure a smooth and scalable onboarding experience. . This focus is ideal for structured, proactive problem-solvers who enjoy bringing clarity to complexity and improving systems sustainably. ➡️ A background in VC, high-growth startups or consulting is a plus. Where this can take you: Careers in fund administration or client and investor operations. Venture Operations Get a front-row seat to how unregulated investment vehicles are executed on our platform. You’ll manage investor onboarding, investment documentation, capital calls, and more - helping us scale deal execution with quality and speed across jurisdictions, focusing on process efficiency and end-to-end automation across jurisdictions. This is for you if you’re a fast learner, clear communicator, and want to work at the intersection of product and operations. ➡️ A background in VC, high-growth startups or consulting is a plus. Where this can take you: Careers in venture capital operations, business development or project management. Fund Accounting Take ownership of investor reporting cycles, a regulatory requirement for funds in each of our jurisdictions. You’ll work with large datasets, external accountants and our product team to help ensure that investors receive accurate, timely, and clear reports. Perfect for structured and detail-driven minds who can turn complex data into meaningful, compliant communications. ➡️ Strong Excel skills and a background in finance or or accounting are a plus. Where this can take you: Careers in fund accounting, financial reporting or finance operations. What You Bring Previous experience in a fast-paced environment (VC, consulting, investment banking, business law, etc.) or an operations-related role, ideally in a fast-paced setting You are a recent graduate or nearing the end of your studies Reliable, detail-oriented, and comfortable taking ownership Curious and proactive mindset - you like to ask “why” instead of just accepting things Understanding of basic private market fundamentals and an interest to dive deep into private asset investing Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English Familiarity with automation and project management tools like Notion, Make, Asana or Retool is a plus Why You’ll Love It Here Make your mark in a mission-driven FinTech startup that values each of its bunchies Be mentored by experienced operators and founders, that take your development seriously Work from an amazing office right in Berlin-Mitte and be part of a welcoming and motivated team Learn fast in a culture that values ownership, creativity, and trust and always strives to empower others Additionally enjoy benefits in mobility, food and learning Take part in a network of people passionate about investment and work closely with the most interesting players in the private market. Benefit from working with a diverse mix of talents, unrivalled energy, and team spirit within a culture of drive and ownership Flexible hours and a hybrid office setup (3 days/week in office) About bunch bunch is building the operating infrastructure for the next generation of private markets. We combine AI-powered automation with deep regulatory expertise to replace fragmented spreadsheets and manual processes with one integrated platform across the fund lifecycle, purpose-built for private markets heading toward $32 trillion in Assets Under Management. We've 4x our ARR in 2025, crossed 150 fund managers and 12,000 LPs on the platform, and just closed our $35M Series B in May 2026. We're looking for ambitious people who want real ownership of hard problems, and who care about building infrastructure that actually matters to the people using it. ____ At bunch, we're committed to an inclusive environment where diversity is valued and celebrated. We provide equal opportunities to all qualified applicants. We process personal data in line with applicable laws (including GDPR). See our Privacy Policy for details on your rights and how to reach us. Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
