    schema:description "Join us in driving connectivity forward! At One Mobility Group, we bridge worlds—combining nearly a century of German automotive engineering precision with the innovation power of the globe's largest electronics and ICT manufacturer. This unique positioning makes us the strategic partner for end-to-end mobility solutions—from initial concept design to large-scale manufacturing. Our comprehensive portfolio spans the full spectrum of electrified mobility, including power distribution systems, high- and low-voltage modules, safety components, and advanced charging solutions. We specialize in integration expertise that seamlessly connects data, power, and sensing – redefining what’s possible in intelligent, connected mobility. At One Mobility, you will join a vibrant international team of 10,500 people, working together in 17 countries across Europe, Asia, North America, the Middle East, and Africa. Step into a culture where inclusivity is the foundation, where your ideas are trusted and supported, your passions are nurtured, and the spirit of collaboration is encouraged. We move fast, think differently, and empower our people to deliver breakthrough solutions. We are looking for Senior Accountant Consolidation & Reporting (m/f/d) at one of our locations in EMEA region - Germany (Reutlingen) Your tasks: Support the preparation of group consolidation in accordance with HGB and IFRS, including monthly, quarterly, and annual consolidated financial statements Perform monthly consolidation of income, expenses, and balances to ensure a consistent and reliable data basis across the group Contribute to internal reporting and prepare insightful ad-hoc analyses and management reports for decision-making purposes Compile, analyze, and interpret financial data for reporting Analyze and reconcile balance sheet and P&L positions as a basis for management decisions Analyze and resolve intercompany differences in close collaboration with group entities Lead and participate in projects to improve accounting processes, systems, and methodologies Degree in Business Administration, Finance, Accounting, or a comparable qualification At least 2-5 years of professional experience in group accounting / consolidation Solid knowledge of accounting standards under HGB and IFRS Experience working with SAP and LucaNet is an advantage Experience in Manufacturing is mandatory (automotive is an advantage) Fluent in English, (both written and spoken) German knowledge is an advantage Strong analytical skills and a structured, detail-oriented working style High affinity for numbers, together with initiative and a solution-driven approach Hands-on mentality, strong sense of responsibility, and enthusiasm for improving processes and systems Our offer: A permanent, full-time position A mixed team of fresh talent and long-standing employees Extensive training and development opportunities A structured induction program An attractive remuneration package Are you interested? We are looking forward to receive your application. If you have any questions in the meantime do not hesitate to contact us. Please apply online in English and use our web portal at onemobility.recruitee.com. One Mobility GmbH Contact person: Zsófia Angyal, Global Recruiting Coordinator email: Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Experienced, fulltime permanent" ;
